.TH GRIDFM 1 "2026-09-05" "gridfm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gridfm \- a keyboard-first terminal file manager with a visual card grid
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gridfm
.RI [ options ] " [directory]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gridfm
presents the filesystem as a responsive grid of cards: directories and
files are navigated spatially with arrow or vim keys, inspected in a
side panel, mutated through a safe operation queue with trash support,
and — on terminals that speak the Kitty graphics protocol — previewed
as image thumbnails.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-icons " mode"
File type representation:
.BR labels ", " unicode ", or " nerdfont "."
Default is taken from the configuration file, else
.BR unicode .
.TP
.BI \-images " mode"
Terminal image thumbnails:
.BR auto ", " on ", or " off "."
.B auto
enables thumbnails on kitty and Ghostty;
.B on
forces them on (for terminals verified to speak the protocol);
.B off
disables them.
.TP
.B \-sidebar
Show the sidebar at start. On by default.
.TP
.B \-inspector
Open the inspector panel at start. Off by default.
.TP
.B \-hidden
Show dot-prefixed entries. Off by default.
.TP
.BI \-sort " mode"
Initial sort:
.BR name ", " size ", " modified ", or " type .
.TP
.BI \-order " dir"
Initial sort direction:
.B asc
or
.BR desc .
.TP
.B \-mouse
Enable mouse clicks and wheel scrolling. Off by default: capturing the
pointer disables the terminal's text selection.
.TP
.BI \-completions " shell"
Print a completion script for
.BR bash ", " zsh ", or " fish
and exit.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.SS Navigation
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
arrows, h j k l|move focus
enter|enter directory / open
backspace|parent directory
alt+left / alt+right|browsing history
pgup / pgdn|page
home / end|first / last
tab|switch grid / sidebar focus
.TE
.SS View
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
/|filter (type to narrow)
.|toggle hidden files
s|sort menu (+ reverse with o)
+ / \-|card size
i|inspector panel
~|sidebar
r|refresh
?|this legend
.TE
.SS Files
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
space|toggle selection
v|range select mode
ctrl+a|select visible
y / x|stage copy / move
p|paste
n / ctrl+d|new file / directory
R|rename
d / D|trash / delete (D types "yes")
b / B|bookmark add / remove
o|open (editor or xdg-open)
c|cancel running operation
e|last operation result
q|quit (confirms while jobs run)
.TE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gridfm/config.toml
Configuration. A missing file means defaults; see
.B README.md
for the schema covering icons, thumbnails, panels, sorting, key
remapping
.RI( [keys] ),
and the color palette
.RI( [theme] ).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/gridfm/bookmarks.toml
Bookmarks, managed with
.B b
and
.BR B .
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/gridfm/thumbs
Bounded thumbnail cache.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on usage or configuration errors.
.SH AUTHORS
The gridfm authors.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
The project README for configuration examples and installation.
